@SAbboushi this looks like #1393, which is fixed on master by #1394 (merged October 29, not in a release yet).

When several assets share one original file (what Photos' Duplicate command creates), the listing moved its offset forward once per original, while iCloud counts assets. The next page then started a few items too early, so the last items of the previous page came back a second time and were reported as "already exists". That matches your log: the same three files, in the same order, right after they were downloaded. `--skip-created-after` doesn't help because the whole library is still listed page by page and filtered locally.

The same bug also skipped one asset of each group that shares an original, so your local count may come out a little higher once you're on a version with the fix. You can try it now with `pip install git+https://github.com/icloud-photos-downloader/icloud_photos_downloader`, or wait for the next release.
